markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Display Pipeline

Before users ever see data on the screen, an app has to make a series of decisions about what data to use, how to process it, and how to display it.

A pipeline starts with raw data, reshapes it for a purpose, and then displays the result to the user.


 <div style="background-color: #e4e2f8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;"> <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 A <strong>pipeline</strong> is a series of steps that you run in order, where the output from one step becomes the input to the next. </p> </div>

---

## How Loops Fit into the Display Pipeline

A display pipeline describes how data moves from storage to the screen.
Loops are what allow the program to process each piece of data systematically at every stage.

### **Steps:**

<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;max-width:900px;margin:auto;">

  <details style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
    <summary style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer;">1. Read: Decide What Data Your App Will Use</summary>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:15px;margin-top:16px;">
      <img src="https://images.code.org/31f147dec60e5cb84e6be34638f4dc3d-image-1768927433873.png" alt="file folder emoji" style="width:20%;max-width:120px;height:auto;border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">

  <div style="flex:1;background:#f7f8fa;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;font-size:14pt;">
        <p style="font-size:12pt;">
          Data is stored in an array or list.<br>
          A loop is prepared to move through the array one element at a time.
        </p>

  <p style="font-size:12pt;">
          <i><b>Loop’s role:</b> Enables access to each item in the dataset.</i>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
    <summary style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer;">2. Transform: Select What Fits Your Purpose</summary>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:15px;margin-top:16px;">
      <img src="https://images.code.org/c58c4f780a34e12135ae97962267c13d-image-1768927841008.png" alt="gear emoji" style="width:20%;max-width:120px;height:auto;border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">

  <div style="flex:1;background:#f7f8fa;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;font-size:14pt;">
        <p style="font-size:12pt;">
          A loop goes through the array and checks each element.<br>
          Conditions, like <code>if</code> statements, inside the loop decide:
        </p>

  <ul>
          <li style="font-size:12pt;">Which items to keep</li>
          <li style="font-size:12pt;">Which items to skip</li>
          <li style="font-size:12pt;">How values should be modified</li>
        </ul>

  <p style="font-size:12pt;">
          <i><b>Loop's role:</b> Applies the same rules consistently to every item.</i>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
    <summary style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer;">3. Render: Display the Data to the User</summary>

<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:15px;margin-top:16px;">
      <img src="https://images.code.org/792cd534bf599b4696528668350410eb-image-1768927535521.png" alt="computer monitor emoji" style="width:20%;max-width:120px;height:auto;border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">

  <div style="flex:1;background:#f7f8fa;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;font-size:14pt;">
        <p style="font-size:12pt;">
          The loop uses the transformed data to update the screen.<br>
          Each iteration adds text, images, or visual elements to the view.<br>
          Formatting and feedback, like colors, messages, and layout, happen here.
        </p>

  <p style="font-size:12pt;">
          <i><b>Loop's role:</b> Turns processed data into visible output, one item at a time.</i>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>

</div>










MARKDOWN
